
Abstraction hides complex internal logic and shows only what the user needs.
Python achieves abstraction mainly through abstract base classes (ABCs) and abstract methods.
ABCs cannot be instantiated and serve as blueprints for subclasses

CODE:-


from abc import ABC, abstractmethod

class Item_abstract(): 
    @abstractmethod
    def print_item_name(self):
       pass

class Shirt(Item_abstract):
    def show(self):
        print("show of the shirt class")

obj = Item_abstract()
obj.print_item_name()
obj2 = Shirt()
obj2.show()
